{
  "name": "Nurture real estate leads from Follow Up Boss signals with Claude and Gmail",
  "flow": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "config_your_name",
            "value": "Your name — signs every outgoing message"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_your_email",
            "value": "you@example.com"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_your_company",
            "value": "Your company or brokerage"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_timezone",
            "value": "Europe/London"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_quiet_hours_start",
            "value": "21"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_quiet_hours_end",
            "value": "8"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_approval_mode",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_approver",
            "value": "#approvals — a Slack channel, or an email address"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_test_mode",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_schedule",
            "value": "scenario schedule: Signal events (listing feed, rate feed, CRM dates, calendar)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Config (edit me)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "run_at",
            "value": "{{now}}"
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 300,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Detect the reason (runs on the scenario schedule)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "result",
            "value": ""
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 600,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Match leads to the signal (port the rule here)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "result",
            "value": ""
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 900,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Check the guardrails (port the rule here)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "module": "anthropic-claude:createAMessage",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
        "system": "You are the \"Draft the message\" step of the Lead Nurture Automation workflow run by Agentmelt.\nTask: Two to four sentences in the agent's voice that name the reason, reference what the lead said last time, and ask one question. Fair-housing wordlist applied.\n\nRules:\n- No message without a reason the lead would recognise; the model cannot invent one.\n- Frequency cap: at most one touch per lead per 14 days, at most three per quarter.\n- Anyone in an active conversation or an active CRM stage is excluded automatically.\n- Unsubscribe and STOP are honoured on the first word; suppression is written to the CRM.\n- Fair-housing language check on every draft; flagged drafts cannot be sent.\n- Answer only from the data provided in the input. If something is missing, say so in the output instead of guessing.\n- If this step produces a message or a document, put the full text in `draft` (and a `subject` if it is an email); put a one-line summary in `summary`.\n- Set `needs_human` true whenever you are unsure, the input is unusual, or a rule above applies; a person will look at it.\n- Return valid JSON matching the output schema; no prose outside the JSON.\n\nReply with a single JSON object and nothing else: the fields the task needs, plus \"needs_human\" (true when unsure), \"confidence\" (0–1) and \"summary\" (one line).",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Draft the message.\n\nItem (map the fields your source provides here):\n{{4.text}}{{4.body}}{{4.message}}{{4.subject}}{{4.email}}{{4.name}}{{4.data}}"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "max_tokens": "2000",
        "temperature": "0.2",
        "metadata": {}
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1200,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Claude: Draft the message"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "module": "json:ParseJSON",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "json": "{{5.textResponse}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1500,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Parse Claude's JSON: Draft the message"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": null,
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1800,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Gate: Draft the message"
        }
      },
      "routes": [
        {
          "flow": [
            {
              "id": 13,
              "module": "builtin:ThrowWarning",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "message": "Parked for a person — Draft the message: {{6.summary}}"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2100,
                  "y": 0,
                  "name": "Needs a person: Draft the message"
                }
              },
              "filter": {
                "name": "Needs a person?",
                "conditions": [
                  [
                    {
                      "a": "{{6.needs_human}}",
                      "b": "true",
                      "o": "boolean:equal"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "flow": [
            {
              "id": 7,
              "module": "slack:CreateMessage",
              "version": 4,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "channelType": "public",
                "channel": "{{1.config_approver}}",
                "text": "Approve? {{6.summary}}\n\nReply in the thread with APPROVE or REJECT. With config_approval_mode = true nothing is written until the item is re-run with approved = true.",
                "parseText": false,
                "mrkdwn": true
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2100,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Slack approval: Approve or auto-send"
                }
              },
              "filter": {
                "name": "Continue",
                "conditions": [
                  [
                    {
                      "a": "{{6.needs_human}}",
                      "b": "true",
                      "o": "boolean:notequal"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 12,
              "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": null,
              "mapper": null,
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2400,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Approval gate: Approve or auto-send"
                }
              },
              "routes": [
                {
                  "flow": [
                    {
                      "id": 11,
                      "module": "builtin:ThrowWarning",
                      "version": 1,
                      "parameters": {},
                      "mapper": {
                        "message": "Approval requested. Re-run the item with approved = true (or set config_approval_mode = false) to write it back."
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 2700,
                          "y": 150,
                          "name": "Waiting for approval: Approve or auto-send"
                        }
                      },
                      "filter": {
                        "name": "Approval mode on",
                        "conditions": [
                          [
                            {
                              "a": "{{1.config_approval_mode}}",
                              "b": "true",
                              "o": "text:equal"
                            }
                          ]
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "flow": [
                    {
                      "id": 8,
                      "module": "google-email:ActionSendEmail",
                      "version": 2,
                      "parameters": {},
                      "mapper": {
                        "to": [
                          "{{7.email}}"
                        ],
                        "subject": "{{6.subject}}",
                        "html": "{{6.draft}}",
                        "attachments": []
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 2700,
                          "y": 300,
                          "name": "Gmail: Send and log"
                        }
                      },
                      "filter": {
                        "name": "Approved or approval mode off",
                        "conditions": [
                          [
                            {
                              "a": "{{1.config_approval_mode}}",
                              "b": "false",
                              "o": "text:equal"
                            }
                          ],
                          [
                            {
                              "a": "{{1.approved}}",
                              "b": "true",
                              "o": "boolean:equal"
                            }
                          ]
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "id": 9,
                      "module": "google-email:TriggerNewEmail",
                      "version": 2,
                      "parameters": {
                        "searchType": "simple",
                        "criteria": "UNSEEN",
                        "markSeen": false,
                        "maxResults": 1
                      },
                      "mapper": {},
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 3000,
                          "y": 300,
                          "name": "Gmail: Stop on reply"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "id": 10,
                      "module": "google-sheets:addRow",
                      "version": 2,
                      "parameters": {},
                      "mapper": {
                        "from": "drive",
                        "mode": "select",
                        "values": {
                          "0": "{{6.summary}}"
                        },
                        "sheetId": "Sheet1",
                        "spreadsheetId": "",
                        "includesHeaders": true,
                        "insertDataOption": "INSERT_ROWS",
                        "valueInputOption": "USER_ENTERED",
                        "insertUnformatted": false
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 3300,
                          "y": 300,
                          "name": "Google Sheets: Report"
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "instant": false,
    "version": 1,
    "scenario": {
      "roundtrips": 1,
      "maxErrors": 3,
      "autoCommit": true,
      "autoCommitTriggerLast": true,
      "sequential": false,
      "slots": null,
      "confidential": false,
      "dataloss": false,
      "dlq": false,
      "freshVariables": false
    },
    "designer": {
      "orphans": []
    },
    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          1
        ],
        "content": "## Nurture real estate leads from Follow Up Boss signals with Claude and Gmail\n\nReal-estate agents whose long-term leads go cold because nobody has a reason to write.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: A new listing in the CRM or MLS feed, a rate change from your lender's feed, an anniversary or birthday in the CRM, or a lead going quiet for N days each start a run for the leads they affect.\n1. Detect the reason\n2. Match leads to the signal\n3. Check the guardrails\n4. Draft the message\n5. Approve or auto-send\n6. Send and log\n7. Stop on reply\n8. Report\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Follow Up Boss / kvCORE / HubSpot, Gmail / Outlook, Slack.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the signal types and your voice rules in the Config node; swap Follow Up Boss for kvCORE or HubSpot.\nGuardrail to keep: No message without a reason the lead would recognise; the model cannot invent one.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/lead-nurture-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}